@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

# =============================================================
#  Dependency injection: Singleton vs Scoped vs Transient
#  Start the API (F5), then send these requests in order.
# =============================================================

### DI1. Log in (200 OK with the access token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara.ahmed@example.com",
  "password": "Clinic2026!"
}

### DI2. Register a patient (201 Created; random passport so it never clashes)
# @name newPatient
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Imran",
  "lastName": "Qureshi",
  "dateOfBirth": "1987-09-03",
  "gender": "Male",
  "maritalStatus": "Married",
  "nationalityCode": "IN",
  "identityType": "Passport",
  "identityNumber": "P{{$randomInt 1000000 9999999}}",
  "mobileNumber": "+9198{{$randomInt 10000000 99999999}}",
  "address": { "line1": "5 Charminar Road", "city": "Hyderabad" }
}

### DI3. Transient: FileNoGenerator builds the file number (200 OK, CF-2026-...)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/{{newPatient.response.body.$.id}}/file-number
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### DI4. Scoped: ICurrentUser fills DeactivatedBy from the token (204 No Content)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/{{newPatient.response.body.$.id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### L1. Instance ids per lifetime (send it twice and compare)
# singleton: the same in every response, until the app restarts
# scoped:    the same for endpoint and reporter (one request), new on the next request
# transient: different for endpoint and reporter, and new on every request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diagnostics/lifetimes
